      "writtenOn": "2023-05-16T23:21:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The proper way to do that is packing all fpsensor_state variables into a \"context\", and passing it around.\n\nThis sounds good and is something I have wanted to clean up for a long time.\n\n\u003e But I don\u0027t want to do a huge refactor now, because that may introduce too much risk.\n\nLet\u0027s go ahead and try it. I don\u0027t think it will introduce much risk if we keep the refactor in a separate CL (or multiple depending on how large it is). There is more risk if we try to refactor later, since we are adding more code that depends on global variables/state. (Also see [this comment](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/4511814/comment/69f11e6e_d2393261/)).",
