      "writtenOn": "2023-05-30T17:57:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e But the idea of test/fpsensor_auth_crypto_mock.c doesn\u0027t work.\n\nWhat I mean is that if you are going to add a `mocklist` file, then separate out the tests that require a mock into a separate test file. For example, [here](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/4511814/42/test/fpsensor_auth_crypto.mocklist) you add a `mocklist` for `test/fpsensor_auth_crypto.cc`. However, the existing tests (e.g., `test_fp_create_ec_key_from_pubkey`) do not require a mock, so we can keep them in a separate test file from the set of tests that do require a mock (e.g., `test_fp_encrypt_decrypt_data`).",
